# Desktop frontend (Svelte 5 + Tauri)

- Svelte 5 runes only: `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, `$props`. No legacy
  `export let` / reactive `$:` statements.
- All backend calls go through `desktop/src/lib/api.ts` (thin `invoke` wrappers);
  components never call `@tauri-apps/api` `invoke` directly.
- Keep TS types in `desktop/src/lib/types.ts` mirroring the Rust structs used
  for IPC. Update both sides together when the contract changes.
- New Tauri commands must be registered in `desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs`
  (`tauri::generate_handler!`); custom app commands don't need a capabilities
  entry.
- Run `npm run check` (svelte-check) after edits — it must report 0 errors.

```ts
// ✅ add a binding in lib/api.ts, then call it from components
export const startRecording = () => invoke<void>("start_recording");
```
